From 3cf2236a0c0d861af346e59c3c1bb8027fe9f8ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReArc Overlay <overlay@rearc.invalid>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:45:18 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 wave 18e: print registry tabs through host-rendered
 PDF

Attach Chromium's printing helpers to browser-less tabs and generate PDFs of the primary document with PrintViewManager/PdfPrintJob for the host to print with NSPrintOperation or save as PDF. Registry tabs never open Chromium's WebUI print preview or system print dialog: scripted, requested and system-dialog print paths complete the page's request (beforeprint/afterprint) and post a host print request instead. One job per tab; navigation, discard and close cancel. ABI 1.28 / bridge 0.30.0; build p75, native PDF bytes/pages, landscape page range, invalid range, busy, window.print request/afterprint and navigation/close cancellation pass.

Last rebased: 2026-11-04 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.74 (d331de35ca).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
